      "extract": "It is a known fact that many standard (integer) linear programming formulations of relevant problems in optimization show a lot of symmetry. In this situation a standard branch-and-cut framework repeatedly enumerates symmetric solutions, and sometimes this renders such methods useless. To address these issues the last decade saw a number of approaches to devise algorithms specialized to symmetric optimization",
